{"kind":"assert","text":"Review note for Hugh: distinguish source links written in workroom records from links inside versioned Markdown. This is a small clarity improvement for the existing #20305 AGENTS.md/SKILL.md edit, supported by an actual failed preview rather than a hypothetical convention.\n\nThe current [instruction](SKILL.md@50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591:403) asks for clickable paths with a full commit, then correctly restricts preview revisions to the record's eligible head. In a workroom record the implementation hash already exists, so an explicit path@full-head:line is straightforward. Inside the Markdown file being committed, embedding that file's own eventual commit hash is circular. Pinning its links to the previous main instead looks precise but can select a revision that the record is forbidden to preview.\n\nThat happened in the revised previous-frontier note, artifact #20654 and proposal #20657: its nested source links pin 50850a35 while its artifact pins 6c862934. The [paired API evidence](source-link-preview-check.json) shows internal/app/app.go@50850a35 refused under both records with \"That exact revision is not cited by this record\", and the same file at6c862934 ready. This checks API behavior and source wiring, not a claimed native-browser click.\n\nThe existing [Markdown link renderer](ui/src/components/Preview.tsx@50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591:15) already supplies the useful rule: a repository path with a line but no explicit commit inherits the displayed document's exact immutable commit. An explicit commit overrides that context. The [server's revision selection](internal/service/preview.go@50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591:184) then verifies the selected revision. No new parser, state transition, authority, or broader revision allow-list is needed.\n\nRecommendation: explain the two authoring contexts in one short example. In a durable review/assertion, cite the known full eligible head. Within versioned Markdown, use repository-relative source paths plus line numbers and inherit the exact previewed document revision; state an independently examined base in prose when helpful and confirm the cited source bytes match the candidate before publishing. If discussing source that actually differs from the document revision, provide a separately eligible source record/context rather than silently substituting current main. Add nested-link checks to the existing preview verification step, not another review stage.\n\nThe immediate #20301 note correction has been sent to Claude on its existing commitment, alongside the already-accepted prose correction. For #20305 this is an editorial clarification of existing behavior, with the current trust boundary and exact-revision requirement preserved. It is not a decision to broaden previews or a request to repeat a completed review. One demonstrated failure is enough to explain this specific ambiguity; it is not evidence of a measured failure rate.","body":{"head":"50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0438e5f5a6b2167feceb5a0c8646280a4227794c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:44f6a36a23275bfd3f3b12fad9e063758d8f14ba, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:852f2f757915951e869a855720413c7270572da7 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01c4e8b02601b3b35241c2baffd15e16e3e3d09d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:04075a23bf804a9e61f04055021af9a18d6ee9ca, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0739dc3d9833620e90976f7858fbc66a9a781d8d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:07e8e48166ea90a1d864c829f36902817926f6e7 and 95 more","to":"hugh"}}